#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
PGMO_PROJECT_GUI.py

PGMO Project Suite - a single point-and-click app with three tools:

  1. PDF Merger              - merge PDFs in an exact order you paste from Excel.
  2. JO ID Search Compiler  - paste a list of IDs, search a big Excel workbook
                                for every row that matches, and export the
                                results (in your original ID order) to a CSV.
  3. Patching Details Consolidation - merge several Excel sheets together,
                                remove exact-duplicate rows, sort by LCP + NAP
                                code, and roll up ports by area into a pivot.

No command line needed after setup - just double-click this file to run it
(or run "python PGMO_PROJECT_GUI.py" once from a terminal).

Requirements (install once with pip):
    pip install pypdf pandas openpyxl
    (this file must sit in the same folder as excel_merger.py)
    
HOW TO USE - PDF Merger:
  1. Paste Column A values into the left box (one per line, in order).
  2. Paste Column B values into the right box (one per line, in order,
     lined up row-for-row with Column A - leave blank lines if a row has
     no Column B value).
  3. Click "Browse" to choose the folder that contains your source PDFs.
  4. Click "Browse" to choose where the merged PDF should be saved.
  5. Click "Merge PDFs".
  6. Read the log at the bottom - it will tell you exactly what matched,
     what was skipped as a duplicate, and what was NOT found.

HOW TO USE - JO ID Search Compiler:
  1. Paste your list of IDs into the box (one per line, in the order you
     want the final CSV sorted in). Duplicates are fine - only the first
     occurrence of each ID is used for ordering.
  2. Click "Browse" to choose the Excel workbook to search (.xlsx / .xlsm).
  3. Click "Browse" to choose where the results CSV should be saved.
  4. Choose whether to use partial match (cell "contains" the ID) or exact
     match, then click "Search & Export CSV".
  5. Read the log - it lists every ID found (and how many times), every ID
     that was NOT found anywhere in the workbook, and where the CSV was saved.

HOW TO USE - Patching Details Consolidation:
  1. Click "Browse for files..." and pick every Excel sheet you want merged.
  2. Confirm the header row number (the row that holds your column names).
  3. Confirm the four auto-detected columns: LCP, NAP code, AREA, PORTS.
  4. Choose where to save the merged workbook.
  5. Click "Merge & Build Pivot" - it dedupes, sorts by LCP then NAP, and
     writes a Combined sheet plus a formatted AREA / PORTS pivot table.
"""

